          "ruleId": "PRREV-AGY",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "scripts/ci.sh step 4 fails because `cargo test --test property_tests` fails with 'no test target named property_tests in default-run packages'."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": ""
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "failure_scenario": "CI cannot complete because the property_tests target is not in the default-run packages (the workspace root), breaking the hardcoded cargo test command in ci.sh.",
            "source": "agy gemini-3.1-pro-high: bash scripts/ci.sh",
            "excerpt": "bash scripts/ci.sh",
            "excerpt_sha256": "12208895bfe2b54edff1d36a14e49d1b70a3971c43aa7bb0cb527659eabe3ec3",
            "disposition": "agreed, pre-existing and out of scope: scripts/ci.sh is byte-identical on origin/main and reachable only via Makefile:777; filed as paiml/aprender#2852"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-AGY",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "`apr serve` silently drops `ignore_eos` during deserialization because `ChatCompletionRequest` in `crates/apr-cli/src/commands/serve/types.rs` lacks the field."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "crates/apr-cli/src/commands/serve/types.rs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 422
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "failure_scenario": "The measurement harness sends a request with `ignore_eos: true`, but `apr serve` ignores it. The generation stops early on EOS, returning fewer tokens than `n_predict`. The harness then fails the run under PP-28 because `completion_tokens != n_predict`.",
            "source": "agy gemini-3.1-pro-high: docs/specifications/PP-LLAMA-001-MASTER.md (PP-28)",
            "excerpt": "docs/specifications/PP-LLAMA-001-MASTER.md (PP-28)",
            "excerpt_sha256": "738fb9654a9bb62b813f817c61356ba04150621cb7b0cdd4e98941b985fbbbb7",
            "disposition": "agreed for the SafeTensors route (serve/safetensors.rs mounts the handler that deserialises into the field-less type; files untouched by this PR); not the measured route — the GGUF/realizar route honours ignore_eos (PERF-039) and every witness slot completed n_predict tokens; filed as paiml/aprender#2853"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-AGY-PRIOR",
          "level": "note",
          "baselineState": "absent",
          "message": {
            "text": "Double counting of staggered joins artificially inflates the in_flight_now metric in cuda_batch_scheduler. (found on e3ab9f90c; fixed in a765c86a5; absent on this head)"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "crates/aprender-serve/src/api/cuda_batch_scheduler.rs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 478
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "failure_scenario": "A batch of size M with staggering will call in_flight.enter() M times initially, then again for each staggered prompt popped from pending_joins, reporting up to 2*M - 1 concurrent requests for a batch that never exceeded M slots. Conversely, recycled slots from rx in PMAT-074 never call enter(), under-counting actual concurrency. This breaks the PP-24 concurrent ladder derivation by overstating the peak_in_flight.",
            "source": "agy gemini-3.1-pro-high on e3ab9f90c: in_flight.enter();",
            "excerpt": "in_flight.enter();",
            "excerpt_sha256": "f9d948ca49073781dc09b02da70170dc2c1e678bb700e4b0db62d29ad33ce490",
            "disposition": "run 1: 1 finding (PP-24-in-flight-double-count), cited, re-verified by the primary reviewer by reading cuda_batch_scheduler.rs, fixed in a765c86a5 (InFlightCounter::set + BatchInFlight::sync); run 2 on a765c86a5: no findings; run 3 (this block) reviews the PP-26 v3.1 amendment on top"
          }
        }
      ]
